00:11:43.666 --> 00:11:49.866
West starts from a lamb research etcher whose recipe space is on the order of 10 to the power of 23.

00:11:50.646 --> 00:11:56.626
RF power, pressure, gas mix, temperature, and time each move more than one result on the wafer.

00:11:57.066 --> 00:12:02.906
A cleaner critical dimension can thin a film elsewhere. David Fried of Lamb's semiverse group

00:12:02.906 --> 00:12:08.226
described the habit, a process engineer sees the data and reaches for lower pressure and higher

00:12:08.226 --> 00:12:11.966
power because that region fixed the last problem a decade ago.

00:12:12.526 --> 00:12:17.946
Ten to the 23rd is the product of every legal setting on every knob, not a list of 23

00:12:18.266 --> 00:12:18.546
recipes.

00:12:19.166 --> 00:12:23.906
A team samples the neighborhoods it trusts, an optimizer allowed to ignore that history

00:12:23.906 --> 00:12:26.306
can land in a region the plots never suggested.

00:12:26.986 --> 00:12:32.526
Intel's version of the same search from Vika Sharma of Intel Foundry Research is a process

00:12:32.526 --> 00:12:37.946
us with 350 parameters and about 10 to the power of 700 theoretical combinations.

00:12:38.566 --> 00:12:43.126
Engineers and the tool supplier spent about a year reaching a minimally acceptable recipe

00:12:43.126 --> 00:12:46.246
for that layer, then kept going with limited success.

00:12:47.046 --> 00:12:51.526
AI-assisted search started returning better points within a few months, more than one

00:12:51.526 --> 00:12:52.726
of them ahead of the baseline.

00:12:53.286 --> 00:12:55.026
The catch he described is volume.

00:12:55.726 --> 00:12:59.746
Thousands of candidates, each still requiring an expensive silicon experiment.

00:12:59.746 --> 00:13:05.066
The relationships are non-linear, so our ranking earned in one corner of the space misorders

00:13:05.066 --> 00:13:05.906
another corner.

00:13:06.466 --> 00:13:11.486
Two recipes can print the same number in development, and then split once incoming material or

00:13:11.486 --> 00:13:12.586
the tool shifts a little.

00:13:13.146 --> 00:13:14.926
That stability test is the gate.

00:13:15.646 --> 00:13:18.906
Fried's other point is that no single method covers every layer.

00:13:19.486 --> 00:13:24.486
Physical simulation, surrogates, classical machine learning, deep learning, language

00:13:24.486 --> 00:13:27.306
models, and agent setups each do a different job.

00:13:27.306 --> 00:13:30.426
and the work is choosing which one owns which workflow.

00:13:30.966 --> 00:13:33.646
Pass a recommendation from one model to the next

00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:35.926
and the first model's assumptions right along.

00:13:36.566 --> 00:13:39.286
In advance packaging, the same logic meets account

00:13:39.286 --> 00:13:39.986
you can picture.

00:13:40.606 --> 00:13:43.566
Some packages hold hundreds of thousands of interconnects.

00:13:43.986 --> 00:13:46.666
Optical inspection and X-ray collect the images.

00:13:47.406 --> 00:13:50.006
ASE's Ingu Yin Chang put machine vision

00:13:50.006 --> 00:13:52.366
at a thousand shades of gray against the few

00:13:52.366 --> 00:13:53.246
of person's sorts.

00:13:53.846 --> 00:13:55.626
A shade is not a process change.

00:13:55.626 --> 00:14:00.806
The nominated recipe stops being the one to run when it is stable only inside the slice

00:14:00.806 --> 00:14:05.966
of material and tool condition the model already saw, because a non-linear corner will not

00:14:05.966 --> 00:14:07.966
